events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Friday E2E draft release — 2026-09-11\n\nVerdict: `PARTIAL_RELEASE`\n\n## Current state\n\nRelease branch: `release/friday-e2e-2026-09-11`.\n\nExact components integrated:\n\n- Project Office: `66d03a559473bb22b299a24d52cc27728c8093dc` (`PIPELINE_READY`).\n- Local-first runner: `b6a275d5ca3455b2d7de6dc3d23c50fa171c4235` (`RUNNER_READY`).\n- Gemini adapter: `635ed02` (report verdict `AUTH_REQUIRED`; exact resulting commit is recorded by Git).\n- Prometheus slice: this branch, `prometheus/blocker_analysis.py`, protocol `BLOCKER_ANALYSIS/v1`.\n\n## What actually ran\n\nThe Project Office fixture `VIMANA-PILOT` validated successfully. Its founder charter is bounded, synthetic, shadow-only, and its investor status is `PARKED` after an IC recommendation of `RESEARCH_MORE`.\n\nThe runner executed a bounded public synthetic probe using `StubExternal`; it returned a result and a SHA-256 receipt without credentials. The deterministic local runner tests also cover restart/idempotency, privacy routing, free-only billing guard, receipt hashing, and sanitized capability cards. No live Gemini call occurred: the adapter correctly reported `AUTH_REQUIRED`, and no credential was found at the approved boundary. The local Gemma lane remains implemented and private-only, but the live Ollama service was not treated as available without a receipt.\n\nCommands and results:\n\n- `python project-office/validate.py project-office/fixtures/vimana-pilot.json` — valid.\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests` — 124 tests passed.\n- `auth_required(task_id=..., source_digest=..., lease_id=...)` — emits the required Prometheus schema.\n\n## Prometheus diagnosis\n\nThe demonstrated diagnosis is `BLOCKER_ANALYSIS/v1`: process termination or a queued provider job is not semantic completion. The last verified-good transition is founder charter to local-lane submission; the first missing transition is external provider call. Blocker class is `authority`; semantic work is `partial`; retry safety is `continuation_only`; the minimum missing item is a human-authorized Gemini credential; `requires_pasha: true`. Prometheus does not forge completion.\n\n## Butterfly\n\n`BUTTERFLY/v1`\n\n- symptom: a multi-hour commander mandate is naturally represented by infrastructure designed around short task execution.\n- integration_context: the end-to-end release has to continue after a subordinate lane ends or becomes blocked.\n- cocoon: missing distinction between task lease and deadline-bound role/commander lease.\n- possible_feature: persistent authority lease with expiry and child-task lifecycle semantics.\n- cheapest_falsification: restart a commander process after a child reaches `AUTH_REQUIRED` and verify role scope, evidence, and expiry survive without replaying semantic work.\n- decision: `backlog`.\n\n## P(-1) boundaries and rollback\n\nRelaxed only hourly pacing and ordinary mailbox routing for this private release scope. No billing, spending, credentials, MFA changes, force-push, branch-protection bypass, destructive deletion, public publication, or unrelated personal-state access was used. Gemini remains fail-closed pending human authorization. Rollback is to `66d03a5` (the pre-release Project Office head); the release branch can be deleted or closed normally after review. At expiry, stop new work and return routing authority to the normal Market Maker.\n\nQuota/model counters were not exposed by the local tests or runner; no numbers are invented. The supplied manual observation remains the only quota evidence: approximately 85% weekly usage at about 15:30 PT, with 5-hour usage unknown.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-11T23:24:56Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T23:47:58Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"220091951b4c27162a6a3525b4a413a1572e36cd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head